@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+---
+name: permit-status-check
+description: One authorized, disclosed CALL-E status call to a permitting or inspection office that returns a structured permit status and human-owned next action; dry-run by default and never books, pays, submits, or makes legal/code-compliance claims.
+license: MIT
+---
+
+# Permit Status Check
+
+Use this skill when a contractor, architect, or project coordinator has authority to contact a permitting or inspection office about one known permit case and needs a factual status update.
+
+The skill asks for the current permit status, any missing correction or document, inspection readiness, any date the office volunteers, the responsible department/contact, and the smallest administrative next action.
+
+It does **not** impersonate a government official, make legal or code-compliance conclusions, pay fees, submit documents, or book/cancel inspections.
+
+## When To Use
+
+- One known permit or inspection case with a real reference number.
+- The operator is authorized to call the office about that project.
+- The goal is status/exception discovery, not legal advice or autonomous government interaction.
+- A human project team owns every downstream action.
+
+## When Not To Use
+
+- General legal or building-code advice.
+- Filing applications, submitting corrections, paying fees, or booking/canceling inspections.
+- Calling numbers the operator did not provide or authorize.
+- Hidden retries or recurring calls.
+- Any case where the office asks the caller to stop or declines to discuss the permit.
+
+## Required Inputs
+
+- `request_id`: stable local identifier.
+- `company_name`: business disclosed on the call.
+- `project_name`: human-readable project name.
+- `permit_number`: exact permit/application reference.
+- `project_address`: project address supplied by the operator.
+- `jurisdiction`: city/county/authority name.
+- `office_name`: permitting or inspection office.
+- `to_phone_e164`: authorized E.164 number.
+- `region`: explicit CALL-E-supported region.
+- `locale`: supported locale.
+- `authorized`: must be `true`.
+
+## Dry-Run Preview
+
+No CALL-E credentials and no network are required:
+
+```bash
+python3 skills/permit-status-check/scripts/preview.py   --request skills/permit-status-check/assets/sample-permit.json
+```
+
+The preview prints a masked phone number, the exact CALL-E task, a structured-result contract, and a deterministic idempotency key. It never dials.
+
+## CALL-E Goal Template
+
+```text
+You are an AI project-coordination assistant calling on behalf of {company_name}.
+Disclose immediately that you are an AI assistant and not a government official.
+Ask only about permit {permit_number} for {project_name} at {project_address} in {jurisdiction}.
+
+Goal: determine the current permit status, any missing correction or document,
+whether an inspection is required or ready to schedule, any date the office
+volunteers, the responsible department/contact, and the smallest administrative
+next action for the project team.
+
+Do not make legal or code-compliance claims, pay fees, submit documents, schedule
+or cancel an inspection, or make commitments. If the office cannot discuss the
+case or asks you to stop, end the call. Record unknown instead of guessing.
+```
+
+## Structured Result
+
+```json
+{
+  "permit_status": "received | in_review | approved | denied | correction_required | unknown",
+  "missing_items": "string",
+  "inspection_status": "not_required | not_ready | ready_to_schedule | scheduled | unknown",
+  "next_available_date": "YYYY-MM-DD or empty",
+  "next_action": "wait_for_review | submit_correction | provide_document | schedule_inspection | contact_reviewer | human_review | none",
+  "department_or_contact": "string",
+  "follow_up_requested": false,
+  "notes": "string"
+}
+```
+
+A returned `schedule_inspection` value means only that the human project team should consider scheduling. It is not permission for the agent to book anything.
+
+## Live Execution
+
+A live host must:
+
+1. show the exact preview;
+2. confirm authority to contact the office;
+3. confirm AI disclosure;
+4. obtain a fresh explicit live-call intent;
+5. use a deterministic idempotency key;
+6. create at most one CALL-E call for that authorized attempt;
+7. retain and poll the returned call ID instead of creating a duplicate after a timeout;
+8. route the result to a human project queue.
+
+## Cancellation And Idempotency
+
+If the operator cancels before dispatch, do not call. Once CALL-E accepts a call, preserve that call ID and do not redial automatically. Any later follow-up is a new human decision.
+
+See `references/safety.md` and `references/examples.md`.
