+# Examples
+
+## Good: correction required
+
+The office confirms the permit is in review and one revised egress sheet is missing.
+
+```json
+{
+  "permit_status": "correction_required",
+  "missing_items": "Revised egress plan sheet",
+  "inspection_status": "not_ready",
+  "next_available_date": "",
+  "next_action": "submit_correction",
+  "department_or_contact": "Plan Review",
+  "follow_up_requested": false,
+  "notes": "Upload the revised egress sheet through the existing permit portal."
+}
+```
+
+The agent does not upload anything. The human project team decides what to do next.
+
+## Good: ready to schedule
+
+The office says the permit is approved and an inspection may now be requested. Return `inspection_status=ready_to_schedule` and `next_action=schedule_inspection`. Do not book the inspection on this call.
+
+## Good: payment/fee question
+
+If the office mentions an outstanding fee, record it only in `notes` if relevant to status. Do not request card details or attempt payment.
+
+## Refuse: legal interpretation
+
+User asks, "Call the city and tell me whether our design complies with the code."
+
+Do not use this skill. Permit Status Check retrieves administrative status; it does not provide legal or code-compliance conclusions.
+
+## Refuse: autonomous booking
+
+User asks, "Call and book the first inspection slot you can get."
+
+Do not use this skill to book. It may learn that scheduling is available, then return `schedule_inspection` for a human to review.
