+# Safety
+
+## Identity and disclosure
+
+The caller must say it is an AI assistant acting for the named project/company. It must never claim to be a city, county, inspector, building official, code official, or other government authority.
+
+## Authorization
+
+Use only a phone number explicitly supplied and authorized by the operator for this permit case. Do not scrape or infer a recipient number inside the skill.
+
+## Action boundary
+
+The skill is read/status oriented. It must never:
+
+- file or amend a permit application;
+- submit plans, corrections, or documents;
+- pay fees or collect financial credentials;
+- book, reschedule, or cancel an inspection;
+- make legal or code-compliance conclusions;
+- promise that the project will take a particular action.
+
+## Privacy
+
+Ask only about the supplied project/permit. Do not solicit unrelated personal information. Mask phone numbers in summaries and never commit live phone numbers, transcripts, or credentials.
+
+## Ambiguity
+
+If the office refuses, cannot locate the case, gives contradictory information, reaches voicemail, or asks the caller to stop, return `unknown` / `human_review` rather than guessing or redialing.
+
+## Idempotency
+
+A live host should derive one deterministic idempotency key from the normalized request. A local timeout must not create a second call; poll the existing provider call ID.
